![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `loadFont` function from `@remotion/google-fonts` (when imported per-font) accepts only a single options object as its argument. Passing `"normal"` as the first argument is incorrect and will cause the actual options object (containing `weights` and `subsets`) to be ignored, as it will be treated as the second argument which the function does not use.

```suggestion
const { fontFamily, waitUntilDone } = loadFont({
  weights: ["400", "700"],
  subsets: ["latin"],
});
```
